---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Review status">
	<div class="wrap doc">
		<nav class="sidebar" aria-label="Features">
			<div>
				<span class="side-group">Triage</span>
				<a href="/features/review-status/" aria-current="page">Review status</a>
				<span class="side-item">Diff stats</span>
				<span class="side-item">Idle PRs</span>
				<span class="side-item">Reviewer load</span>
			</div>
			<div>
				<span class="side-group">Reviewing code</span>
				<span class="side-item">Collapse generated files <small>Soon</small></span>
				<span class="side-item">Folder diff stats <small>Soon</small></span>
				<span class="side-item">Weighted review progress <small>Soon</small></span>
			</div>
			<div>
				<span class="side-group">Discussing</span>
				<span class="side-item">Quick comments</span>
				<span class="side-item">Conventional Comments <small>Soon</small></span>
				<span class="side-item">Unresolved conversations <small>Soon</small></span>
			</div>
			<div>
				<span class="side-group">Reading</span>
				<span class="side-item">Ticket links <small>Soon</small></span>
				<span class="side-item">Image modal</span>
				<span class="side-item">Before/after slider <small>Soon</small></span>
			</div>
		</nav>

		<main class="doc-main">
			<div class="doc-head">
				<p class="crumbs"><a href="/features/">Features</a> / Triage</p>
				<h1>Review status</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Where each pull request stands for you, on every row of the PR list. You stop opening PRs just to find out
					whether you already reviewed them.
				</p>
				<div class="tags" style="font-size: 13px">
					<span class="tag">Appears in: PR list</span>
					<span class="tag tag-token">Needs token</span>
					<span class="tag tag-on">On by default</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<figure class="prlist" style="margin: 0; box-shadow: none" aria-label="PR rows with a review status badge">
				<div class="pr-row" style="border-top: 0">
					<div class="pr-main">
						<span class="pr-title">feat: OpenTelemetry tracing for task execution</span
						><span class="pr-meta">#3077 opened last week by caseycs</span>
					</div>
					<span class="status s-requested" style="width: 190px; font-size: 13px"
						><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Review requested</span
					>
				</div>
				<div class="pr-row">
					<div class="pr-main">
						<span class="pr-title">fix: preserve dotenv declaration order</span
						><span class="pr-meta">#3078 opened last week by satya-sudo</span>
					</div>
					<span class="status s-rereview" style="width: 190px; font-size: 13px"
						><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Re-review</span
					>
				</div>
				<div class="pr-row">
					<div class="pr-main">
						<span class="pr-title">feat(input): add search and scrolling to choice prompts</span
						><span class="pr-meta">#3071 opened 2 weeks ago by vmaerten</span>
					</div>
					<span class="status s-changes" style="width: 190px; font-size: 13px"
						><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Changes requested</span
					>
				</div>
				<div class="pr-row">
					<div class="pr-main">
						<span class="pr-title">refactor(watch): detect filesystem changes with fsbroker</span
						><span class="pr-meta">#3064 opened last month by andreynering</span>
					</div>
					<span class="status s-outdated" style="width: 190px; font-size: 13px"
						><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Approved · new commits</span
					>
				</div>
			</figure>

			<section class="doc-section">
				<h2>What each status means</h2>
				<dl class="meanings">
					<dt class="s-requested">Review requested</dt>
					<dd>You are asked and have not reviewed yet.</dd>
					<dt class="s-rereview">Re-review</dt>
					<dd>You reviewed, then the author pushed or asked you again.</dd>
					<dt class="s-changes">Changes requested</dt>
					<dd>You asked for changes and nothing has moved since.</dd>
					<dt class="s-outdated">Approved · new commits</dt>
					<dd>You approved, and commits landed after your approval.</dd>
				</dl>
				<p class="muted" style="font-size: 15px">A plain approval gets no badge: GitHub already shows it.</p>
			</section>

			<section class="doc-section">
				<h2>Settings</h2>
				<div class="panel settings">
					<div>
						<span style="font-weight: 600">Badge placement</span
						><span>Right column (default) or the grey line under the title. Shared by all PR list badges.</span>
					</div>
					<div><span style="font-weight: 600">Turn off</span><span>Options › Features › Review status</span></div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="doc-section">
				<h2>Good to know</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>Statuses are fetched again on every visit, so they are never stale.</li>
					<li>A review you started but did not submit counts as no review.</li>
					<li>Needs a token with read access to <i>Pull requests</i>.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<nav class="pager" aria-label="Next and previous feature">
				<a class="panel" href="/features/"><small>Back to</small>All features</a>
				<a class="panel" href="/#demo"><small>See it live</small>Demo on the home page</a>
			</nav>
		</main>
	</div>
</Layout>
